# Copy this file to .env.test. Like .env, it is git-ignored.
#
#   Windows PowerShell:  Copy-Item .env.test.example .env.test
#   macOS / Linux:       cp .env.test.example .env.test
#
# Read only while the tests run: Vitest sets NODE_ENV=test, and
# apps/api/src/config/env.ts loads this file before .env when it sees that.
# Anything not set here falls through to .env.
#
# The test suite empties every table between test cases. It must therefore
# never point at the database you develop against. Two things enforce that:
# the database name below, and a check in apps/api/test/helpers/database.ts
# that refuses to truncate a database whose name does not end in _test.
#
# The database does not have to exist yet — the test harness creates it on
# first run and applies the migrations to it. It only needs the PostgreSQL
# container to be up:  docker compose up -d postgres

# Same server, same credentials as .env, different database.
# The password must match POSTGRES_PASSWORD in your .env.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://vitalink:change_me_locally@localhost:5432/vitalink_test?schema=public"
